{"id": 15217, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:29:54.250315+00:00", "text": "q1\ngiven a graph (undirected)\nsum over all nodes v  of f(v)\nwhere f(v)  = num of connected components after removing v from the graph and keeping the rest intact\n\ntoh har test case ke liye ye sum nikalna tha\nconstraints 10^5-10^6  ke around the", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": {"id": 14992, "text": "plutus quant OA ke questions bhej do", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
{"id": 15218, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:30:07.823569+00:00", "text": "q2\n\ngiven a tree undirected\nand each node of tree has value 1 or 2 or 3\ntell the min number of splitting needed such that no components has ((node product)%6)==0", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": null, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
{"id": 15219, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:30:21.428025+00:00", "text": "q3 \n2<=k<=6\ngiven k strings \nand each string length can be 10^7 (i am not sure of this)\nfind the longest common substring(not subsequence) across all the strings and return its length and not the string", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": {"id": 14995, "text": "Guwahati me ho chuka kyaa?", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
{"id": 15220, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:30:36.684367+00:00", "text": "q4 fir ek greedy ka question tha jo dikhra tha ki greedy se hi hoga mtlb usme constraints bohot high the and dp feasible nhi tha", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": {"id": 14995, "text": "Guwahati me ho chuka kyaa?", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
{"id": 15221, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:31:08.539869+00:00", "text": "q6 Given that 52 cards and per game it costs you 3 dollars to play the game. Game ends when you get spade then heart. You draw cards without replacement.\nFor every spade you get 3 dollars\nFor every heart you get 2 dollars\nFor club/diamonds you lose 1 dollarr\n\nTell me if you should play the game or nott", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": {"id": 14995, "text": "Guwahati me ho chuka kyaa?", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
{"id": 15222, "group": "plutus-research-oa", "sent_at": "2026-10-28T16:31:28.391152+00:00", "text": "5\natm\ngiven an atm \ndo type ki queries thi\n250 -1 -1 -1 -1 -1 (withdraw query) (here 250 is the amt to be withdrawn)\n-1 1 0 0 1 1(deposit query) (here -1 imply deposit fir 5 numbers h number of notes of 20, 50,100,200,500)\n\nnow you can only extract notes from highest to lowest\nand you must extract the notes if they are present\n\n\neg 600 withdraw krne h \nand abhi bank mai [20:0 , 50:1 ,100:0 ,200:3, 500:1 ]\nthen you will extract 500 first\nfir 100 more needed now you cannot extract as no 100 note is present and remaining 50 and 20 cannot also fulfill this\nso you return -1 -1 -1 -1 -1\nelse if you can fulfill you return counts of each notes you extracted\n\nand you will only change balance in atm if money can and is actually extracted otherwise no money is extracted\n\nthis was more of a implementation based question", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": {"id": 14992, "text": "plutus quant OA ke questions bhej do", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
